Hi, Meijun,

I am glad it worked.
I assume that there is a way to make it not constrain the first factor loading to 1, but I do not know exactly how. Based on the report of `lavaan`, v. 0.6-18 <https://lavaan.ugent.be/history/dot6.html>, I tried to use the syntax `F=~l1*NA*x1+x2+x3+x4` with the `HolzingerSwineford1939` dataframe and it worked. Check if it works in your case. <http:///>

Best,
Yago

